{
	"name": "Citrine Serpent",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/snake-fangs-bite-green-yellow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Resembling Tiny snakes made entirely out of a translucent, pale yellow crystal, citrine serpents are often found coiled around deposits of crystalline rock, where they are said to vibrate protective energies into the area they occupy. Adventurers who happen upon a citrine serpent may attempt a DC 15 Animal Handling check to harvest [[/r 1d4]] pieces of crystal from its lair. A DC 15 Medicine or Nature check reveals that the crystals a citrine serpent touches are imbued with the ability to resist poisons. Creatures who have a piece of this crystal on their person have advantage on their saving throw to resist contact or injury poisons. Once the crystal has been used to negate the effects of a poison, it loses all protective properties.</p><p>Citrine serpents who are removed from their rocky homes—and thus cannot vibrate their excess energy into other crystals—are overwhelmed by their own protective forces and crystallize into solid citrine within 24 hours.</p>",
